# Faebloom Trick when an opponent controls no creature: the two Faeries are still created, and the reflexive ability has no
# legal target (Bot1's own Faeries are not creatures "an opponent controls"), so it is never put on the stack (a bare
# ! Bot1.Target would fail if a target were asked) and nothing is tapped: Bot1's Faeries stay untapped. Bot2 controls a
# Mox (an artifact, not a creature), which stays untapped.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Faebloom Trick
Island x3
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Jet
Swamp x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Faebloom Trick.Cast
! Bot1.Target
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Mox Ruby; Mox Pearl; Faerie Token; Faerie Token
Bot1.Battlefield.Faerie Token#1.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Faerie Token#2.Tapped = false
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Jet
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Tapped = false
Bot1.Graveyard = Faebloom Trick
Stack.Count = 0
